          "itemId": "gram-02",
          "content": {
            "rule": "Present Simple Tense for Daily Routines",
            "explanation": "Add '-s' or '-es' to the base verb when the subject is he, she, or it. Verbs ending in ch, sh, x, ss, or o take '-es'. For I, you, we, and they, use the base form.",
            "example": "He goes to school at 8 a.m.",
